    title: "北韓駭客利用假求職手法滲透海外企業，透過合法員工身份進行內部威脅",
    summary: "資安業者 Huntress 揭露北韓駭客組織利用「假求職」的非傳統手法滲透海外企業。攻擊者不透過惡意程式，而是冒用或偽造身分文件，透過正規的徵才管道應徵多領域（如 IT、醫療、業務、行銷）的職位。一旦成功受聘，這些受控制人員便能合法取得企業的帳號、設備及內部系統權限。Huntress 發現，這些人員可能利用 VPN、代理伺服器或 PiKVM 等設備隱藏真實位置，並以內部員工身份進行活動，從而竊取企業資料、部署惡意程式或進行勒索。這種行為使得企業面臨難以被傳統資安工具偵測的內部威脅。Huntress 今年已協助確認數名疑似與北韓相關的工作人員，其中包含在澳洲醫療機構任職的案例。企業應提高警覺，強化對內部人員入職流程的背景調查與監控。",
    tags: ["Huntress", "北韓駭客", "假求職", "內部威脅", "供應鏈安全", "OT/ICS"],
    title_en: "North Korean Hackers Infiltrate Overseas Companies Using Fake Job Applications, Creating Internal Threats",
    summary_en: "Cybersecurity firm Huntress has revealed that North Korean hacking groups are using the non-traditional method of 'fake job applications' to infiltrate overseas companies. Instead of using malicious programs, the attackers pose as or forge identification documents to apply for positions across various domains (such as IT, healthcare, business, and marketing) through legitimate recruitment channels. Once successfully hired, these controlled individuals can legally obtain corporate accounts, equipment, and internal system access. Huntress found that these individuals may use devices like VPNs, proxy servers, or PiKVMs to conceal their true locations and operate as internal employees, thereby stealing corporate data, deploying malware, or conducting ransomware attacks. This behavior creates an internal threat that is difficult for traditional cybersecurity tools to detect. Huntress has confirmed several suspected North Korea-linked employees this year, including a case involving an individual working at a healthcare institution in Australia. Companies should heighten their vigilance and strengthen background checks and monitoring processes for internal personnel onboarding.",
    tags_en: ["Huntress", "North Korean Hackers", "Fake Job Applications", "Internal Threat", "Supply Chain Security", "OT/ICS"],
