    summary_en: "Ubuntu has officially released 24.04.5 LTS, the latest point release for its Long Term Support (LTS) series. This version integrates all stable updates from the past few months, aiming to allow newly installed users to complete deployment faster and reduce the amount of package updates required. Technically, 24.04.5 LTS continues to utilize the Hardware Enablement (HWE) stack, which introduces the Linux 7.0 kernel and Mesa 26.0 graphics drivers, providing an improved experience for users running on newer hardware. Furthermore, all derivative versions based on Ubuntu 24.04.5 LTS, including Kubuntu, Ubuntu Budgie, and Ubuntu MATE, have also released corresponding 24.04.5 LTS media. Developers and users should note that while the HWE stack provides foundational support, upgrading GPU drivers remains advisable for gamers or enthusiasts seeking optimal performance and rich functionality.",
