    title: "Apple Watch Series 12 搭載 Audio Intelligence 功能引發隱私爭議：非同意錄音摘要功能受質疑",
    summary: "Apple 在發布 Apple Watch Series 12 時，加入了 Audio Intelligence 功能，包含 Sound Recognition、Music Recognition (Shazam)、Live Rewind 和 Siri Recap 等 AI 音訊處理能力。Live Rewind 功能透過雙按 Digital Crown，可在 Secure Exclave 上處理音訊流，並將最近 15 秒的對話轉為文字，但原始音訊會被丟棄。Siri Recap 則能總結一天的對話，生成高層次的 Apple Intelligence 筆記。儘管 Apple 聲稱這些功能透過發出聲響和視覺提示來「尊重」周圍人，但隱私倡議者仍對其非同意的音訊處理能力表示擔憂。電子前沿基金會 (EFF) 指出，缺乏明確的選擇加入（opt-in）同意權，可能導致人們自我審查，損害對話的自發性和親密性。專家警告，持續監控對話的技術是不可接受的，呼籲使用者謹慎使用此類功能，並關注其對個人對話隱私的潛在侵犯。",
    tags: ["Apple Watch Series 12", "Audio Intelligence", "Siri Recap", "Live Rewind", "Apple Intelligence", "隱私權"],
    title_en: "Privacy Controversy Surrounds Apple Watch Series 12's Audio Intelligence Feature: Questioning Non-Consensual Recording and Summarization",
    summary_en: "When launching the Apple Watch Series 12, Apple introduced the Audio Intelligence feature, which includes AI audio processing capabilities such as Sound Recognition, Music Recognition (Shazam), Live Rewind, and Siri Recap. The Live Rewind function, activated by double-clicking the Digital Crown, processes the audio stream within a Secure Exclave and transcribes the most recent 15 seconds of conversation, though the original audio is discarded. Siri Recap, meanwhile, can summarize a day's conversations to generate high-level Apple Intelligence notes. Although Apple claims these features 'respect' those nearby by issuing audible and visual prompts, privacy advocates remain concerned about its non-consensual audio processing capabilities. The Electronic Frontier Foundation (EFF) points out that the lack of explicit opt-in consent could lead to self-censorship, damaging the spontaneity and intimacy of conversation. Experts warn that technology enabling continuous monitoring of dialogue is unacceptable, urging users to use such features cautiously and to pay attention to their potential infringement on personal conversational privacy.",
    tags_en: ["Apple Watch Series 12", "Audio Intelligence", "Siri Recap", "Live Rewind", "Apple Intelligence", "Privacy"],
    sources: [
      { name: "The Register", url: "https://theregister.com/security/2026/09/10/watch-out-apple-timepiece-can-grab-snippets-of-conversation-without-both-speakers-consent/5295666", lang: "EN" }
    ]
