    title: "司法部（DOJ）在蘋果反壟斷案中取得暫停令，避免被迫向 14 個聯邦機構索取文件",
    summary: "美國司法部（DOJ）在針對蘋果（Apple）的反壟斷訴訟案中，成功獲得了暫停令，暫緩了先前要求其向 14 個聯邦機構索取文件的命令。此案的核心爭議點在於蘋果主張，這些文件能證明其產品差異化和安全措施並非反競爭行為。蘋果尋求的文件來源包括中央情報局（CIA）、國防部（DoD）、聯邦貿易委員會（FTC）等 14 個機構，目的是檢視這些機構在制定智慧型手機政策時如何評估隱私與安全。原先的裁決後，DOJ 提出上訴，要求暫停文件開示令。最終，法官 Linares 判決支持了 DOJ 的請求，認為在等待上訴結果期間，強制要求 14 個機構進行大量工作將「不公平」。這項暫停令讓蘋果有機會回應政府的上訴，隨後 DOJ 也有權提交回覆，最終由法官 Neals 決定是否維持或推翻原先的開示命令。此案的進展顯示，在涉及跨機構資料的重大科技訴訟中，法律程序和證據開示的時機控制至關重要。",
    tags: ["Apple", "DOJ", "反壟斷", "聯邦機構", "法律訴訟", "資料開示"],
    title_en: "DOJ Secures Stay in Apple Antitrust Case, Avoiding Forced Document Requests from 14 Federal Agencies",
    summary_en: "In the antitrust lawsuit against Apple, the U.S. Department of Justice (DOJ) successfully obtained a stay, pausing a previous order that required Apple to provide documents from 14 federal agencies. The core dispute centers on Apple's argument that the requested documents do not prove that its product differentiation and security measures constitute anti-competitive behavior. The documents sought from 14 agencies, including the Central Intelligence Agency (CIA), Department of Defense (DoD), and the Federal Trade Commission (FTC), aim to review how these agencies assess privacy and security when formulating smartphone policies. Following the initial ruling, the DOJ appealed, requesting the stay of the document disclosure order. Ultimately, Judge Linares ruled in favor of the DOJ's request, deeming it",
