    summary_en: "The image editing software GIMP has released version 3.2.6. In addition to containing multiple security patches and general bug fixes, the most significant development is that developers have begun preparing the codebase for a future migration to the GTK4 platform. Although GIMP 3.0 completed the upgrade from GTK2 to GTK3, this update's preparation work demonstrates its continued commitment to modernizing its interface framework. Regarding performance, version 3.2.6 improves performance when loading a large number of fonts, especially when using the text tool and closing the font list. New features include the ability to use the 'Cut' function on layer groups, and support for 'Barrel Rotation' dynamic input using new Wacom pens. Furthermore, this version provides a new package for macOS users. Users are advised to download the latest version from GIMP.org to ensure optimal stability and security.",
