    title: "Intel Xeon 600 與 AMD Threadripper 9000 專業工作站處理器性能深度比較",
    summary: "本文針對 Intel Xeon 600 系列（以 Xeon 678X 為例）與 AMD Ryzen Threadripper 9000 系列（以 Threadripper 9980X 為例）的專業工作站處理器進行了全面的性能比較。測試涵蓋了近 400 種基準測試，並比較了功耗與頻率表現。Xeon 678X 具備 48 核心/96 執行緒，基礎頻率為 2.4GHz，最大 Turbo 頻率達 4.9GHz，功耗為 300W 基礎，360W 最大 Turbo。而 Threadripper 9980X 則擁有 64 個 Zen 5 核心，基礎時脈為 3.2GHz，最大 Boost 時脈高達 5.4GHz，TDP 為 350W。測試環境使用 Ubuntu 26.04 LTS、Linux 7.0 核心和 GCC 15.2 編譯器，並在性能擴展（performance scaling governor）模式下進行。雖然兩款處理器在核心數量和功耗上存在差異，但本次比較旨在評估它們在多種工作負載下的效能與能效表現，為使用者選擇適合的專業工作站平台提供參考。",
    tags: ["Intel Xeon 600", "AMD Threadripper 9000", "Xeon 678X", "Threadripper 9980X", "工作站處理器", "性能比較"],
    title_en: "In-Depth Performance Comparison of Intel Xeon 600 and AMD Threadripper 9000 Professional Workstation Processors",
    summary_en: "This article provides a comprehensive performance comparison of professional workstation processors, specifically the Intel Xeon 600 series (using the Xeon 678X as an example) and the AMD Ryzen Threadripper 9000 series (using the Threadripper 9980X as an example). The tests covered nearly 400 benchmarks and compared power consumption and frequency performance. The Xeon 678X features 48 cores/96 threads, a base frequency of 2.4GHz, and a maximum Turbo frequency of 4.9GHz, with a base power consumption of 300W and a maximum Turbo of 360W. In contrast, the Threadripper 9980X boasts 64 Zen 5 cores, a base clock of 3.2GHz, and a maximum Boost clock reaching 5.4GHz, with a TDP of 350W. The testing environment utilized Ubuntu 26.04 LTS, Linux 7.0 kernel, and GCC 15.2 compiler, conducted in performance scaling governor mode. Although the two processors differ in core count and power consumption, this comparison aims to evaluate their performance and energy efficiency across various workloads, providing users with a reference for selecting an appropriate professional workstation platform.",
