    title_en: "Framework Adjusts Pricing and Issues Refunds Due to Memory Cost Fluctuations",
    summary_en: "Laptop manufacturer Framework announced that due to the significant increase in the cost of LPCAMM2 memory modules, the company has decided to issue refunds and adjust prices for customers who purchased high-end models. Previously, Framework had informed customers in July that ordering 64GB of RAM would only include 32GB, because the pricing from its LPCAMM2 supplier exceeded expectations, causing costs to double. However, Framework later successfully acquired Micron 32GB and 64GB LPCAMM2 memory modules at a lower cost. Consequently, the company announced a price reduction for shipped and partially processed pre-orders, allowing customers who purchased at the peak memory price to receive a difference refund, or to upgrade their memory capacity at a new, lower price. This move highlights the cost volatility pressure facing the hardware supply chain; other manufacturers like Everpure and HPE had previously promised stable pricing, but memory manufacturers often lock in costs through long-term contracts, and even companies like Apple have chosen to raise product prices.",
