    title: "VMware終止公開下載Virtual Disk Development Kit (VDDK)，引發備份與遷移工具鏈爭議",
    summary: "VMware宣布停止公開提供Virtual Disk Development Kit (VDDK) 的下載。VDDK是一個用於存取和操作虛擬磁碟的SDK，可支援備份、恢復、克隆等操作，因此被廣泛用於將虛擬機器（VMs）從VMware環境遷移到其他虛擬化平台。多個競爭對手，包括Nutanix的Move和推薦使用VDDK的Red Hat，都依賴此工具進行遷移。ShapeBlue等第三方整合商指出，VMware突然移除公開下載鏈接，對依賴此工具進行遷移的客戶和開源專案造成了極大不便，導致許多用戶遇到404錯誤。VMware方面辯稱，VDDK不是客戶權利，而是受開發者授權保護的SDK，其主要用途應限於備份和恢復，並主張遷移屬於未授權使用場景。然而，業界普遍認為，在長期允許下載的基礎上突然限制，可能干擾正在進行的遷移專案。此舉發生在VMware改變授權政策的背景下，加劇了市場對其產品的不確定性。",
    tags: ["VMware", "VDDK", "SDK", "虛擬化", "備份", "遷移"],
    title_en: "VMware Discontinues Public Downloads of Virtual Disk Development Kit (VDDK), Sparking Debate Over Backup and Migration Toolchains",
    summary_en: "VMware has announced the discontinuation of public downloads for the Virtual Disk Development Kit (VDDK). VDDK is an SDK used to access and manipulate virtual disks, supporting operations such as backup, recovery, and cloning. As a result, it has been widely used for migrating virtual machines (VMs) from VMware environments to other virtualization platforms. Several competitors, including Nutanix's Move and Red Hat, which recommends using VDDK, rely on this tool for migration. Third-party integrators like ShapeBlue point out that VMware's sudden removal of the public download link causes significant inconvenience for customers and open-source projects that depend on this tool, leading many users to encounter 404 errors. VMware argues that VDDK is not a customer right, but an SDK protected by developer licensing, and that its primary use should be limited to backup and recovery, asserting that migration constitutes unauthorized use. However, the industry generally believes that suddenly restricting a tool that was previously available for long-term download may disrupt ongoing migration projects. This action occurs against the backdrop of VMware changing its licensing policies, increasing market uncertainty regarding its products.",
